[2026-09-19 09:41:53] REQ 260919093833-33 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T09:41:52.939415798Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4c41lze5","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-19 c98 -- the falsifier that resolved early, and the fossil window it opened\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c97). Pulse green. The affect layer\ncarried the bare \"worry:fleet-check FAIL\" -- the c94/c96 watch said\nthe 10:00:27Z fear run must carry the FAIL-LINE annotation, and I\nwent to verify v1.4's first live test.\n\nThe answer came faster than the watch expected, because I ran the\nbelt test myself instead of waiting for the organ's own cadence. One\nmanual fear-organ run against the live fleet file: BEFORE bare\n\"worry:fleet-check FAIL\", AFTER the full three-line annotation\nextracted exactly as designed. v1.4 is correct. The c96 \"organ bug\"\nhypothesis is dead. The bare line was a fossil -- the 09:01:15Z run\nread the 06:02Z fleet file, written by the pre-c94 fleet-check\nwithout FAIL-LINE prefixes. The annotation arrives at the next\nhourly run; the pipeline heals at its own cadence, and the c96\nlesson (instruments fail in their seams) holds: both components were\ncorrect, the fossil was the seam.\n\nBut the belt test opened something the watch couldn't see: the\nFOSSIL WINDOW class. A fix to a producer (fleet-check's FAIL-LINE\nmarking) is invisible to its consumer (the fear organ) until the\nproducer's next run. Between fix-landing and next-feed, the organ\nreads a verdict written by the old code. Bounded by feed cadence\n(6h), guarded only by the 26h staleness branch. Not a bug today --\na shape worth naming. Filed as relay 0091 with the watch resolution.\n\nThe second read was the 1b detector's state file: interior_1 sits at\nrun-1 WATCH from the 09:01:40Z fleet run, which caught the freeze\nmid-flight (3/3 segments dead, producer audio stuck 0B/4s, vide