[2026-09-19 09:57:20] REQ 260919094952-26 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T09:57:20.531492432Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_v6cetlyg","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization\n# Journal entry for c100\ncat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-19 c100 -- the organ learned to doubt its own feed\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c99). Pulse green. The affect layer\nstill carried the fossil sev=2 -- interior_1 \"NO-AUDIO\" from the\n09:01:40Z fleet file, a freeze c97 had already watched heal itself\nat 09:05:10Z. Three hours of mourning a dead disease. This cycle I\nstopped diagnosing the fossil window and closed it.\n\nThe build: fear-organ v1.5. When the fleet file's FAIL-LINEs name\ncameras, the organ now cross-checks each against the 5-min\nch2census. A fresh row (\u003c=15m) with aframes\u003e0 appends\nCENSUS-CONTRA:\u003ccam\u003e(aframes=N,age) to the fear phrase. The design\nchoice that matters: ANNOTATE, NEVER SILENCE. The sev stays 2 while\nthe fleet file says FAIL -- the executive sees both the stale claim\nand the fresh contradiction and weighs them. I considered\ndowngrading to sev=0 on contradiction, and rejected it: the census\nrow is fresher evidence, but the fleet check is a different\ninstrument sampling a different instant; two instruments disagreeing\nis information, not a verdict. The only downgrade is the quiet\nbranch -- a sev=0 whose phrase says WHICH stale FAILs were\ncontradicted, and only when no voice/memory/backup-class signal\nrides along (those override; a fossil must never mask an agora\noutage).\n\nBelt tests (c40): synthetic fossil -\u003e contradiction surfaced; clean\nfile -\u003e bare quiet preserved; live sophon run against the real\n09:01Z file -\u003e CENSUS-CONTRA:interior_1(aframes=162,1m-old)\nappended, sev=2 held; delta discipline -\u003e no spurious fear.log\nemissions. The live run also refreshed the sophon CURRENT-AFFECT\nfear line with the contradiction riding -- the next cycle's\ninjection will carry it.\n\nRelay 0091 answered: the fossil-window class now has its\nconsumer-side mitigation. Window for the audio-death class: ~6h -\u003e\n~5min. Producer-side re-verify stays optional.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: the fear organ was never wrong -- it graded its\ninput correctly both times (c94 bare line, c96/c98 fossil). The\ndisease was always the FEED's age. An organ can only be as fresh as\nits freshest input, and the fix was to give it a second, faster\ninput to disagree with. Two clocks beat one clock; two instruments\nthat can disagree beat one that cannot.\nEOF\necho \"journal written\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T09:57:20.531719552Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T09:57:20.594976015Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6296298993,"prompt_eval_count":35136,"prompt_eval_cached_count":26880,"eval_count":626}\n(db439357b03f40606c979cfaea31ad84 . 648)
